@joemechlinski Same lesson here, so I changed who reads first.

Hand, my Grok Bot chief of staff, goes through the overnight output before I'm up. A fleet digest lands at 7:35, and the inbox checks only ping me when something actually needs me.

What are your 3?

Money Back, Amazon edition: this weekend a lot of people had an AI agent go through their old Amazon orders, and some found real money.

@cstanley had Grok Bot go through all of his Amazon orders looking for refunds that were never issued. It found $590.62 in missing refunds over several years, opened a support chat, talked to customer service, and got them to agree to issue the refunds. What it means: returns that never got credited add up quietly, and checking years of orders is exactly the boring work an agent can do.
https://t.co/e1MujdCkHo

@trevin used Grok Bot with his Amazon order history export and it found $892 he's owed since 2017 under a class action. He shared his steps: type "request my data" in the Amazon app search to get your order history (his link came by email in 30 minutes), upload the zip, have the bot find the class action email in your inbox (his was in spam, which is why he never knew), have it work out which groups you're in and which purchases qualify, then ask it to file. What it means: the email that matters may be sitting in your spam folder.
https://t.co/ZLh2y1eD5v

@leerob says Grok Bot saved him $100 from Amazon incorrectly charging him. He dropped a post into the chat, and the bot dug through his email, filled out the form and submitted it. What it means: you don't need to understand the form, just hand over the starting point.
https://t.co/ZGQnNpTMlc

A careful setup from @Michael_Fenech_: let your agent help with money without ever being allowed to move it. He splits it into three levels. See it: read-only access to receipts, bills and subscriptions, with a weekly money review. Prepare it: drafts of invoices, cancellations and negotiation emails, with nothing sent or bought automatically. Approve it: every payment, refund or transfer needs his explicit yes. What it means: the agent does the digging, you keep the final say.
https://t.co/zgk495p6Sz

Try it: download your Amazon order history and ask your agent to find returns that were never refunded. Have it show you what it finds and wait for your yes before it contacts support or files anything.

@elonmusk I already did this. My Grok bot got me a £360 hoover for £160.

Got a massive black Friday deal, then it signed up for the newsletter, applied a 10% discount code, and unsubscribed afterwards.

